{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition","id":1436756,"title":"Thoughts about improving the quality of mortal opposition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-24T00:11:29-08:00","id":1436756,"title":"Thoughts about improving the quality of mortal opposition","content":"So, I've been reading my way through &quot;My Problem With Chargen&quot; and enjoying it and it gave me a bunch of thoughts about how part of Exalted's base framework could be reworked to make mortal antagonists, animal as well as human, more mechanically interesting, differentiated, and challenging to younger Exalts.<br /> <br /> Here's the basics:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ordinary mortals are the vast majority of characters. Heroic mortals are those mortals with a spark of greatness, able to go beyond the efforts of others. The Exalted are all chosen from among the ranks of Heroic mortals.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The only resource that ordinary mortals have access to is Willpower and they usually don\u2019t have much of that. Willpower goes from 1 to 5 dots and is used for extreme effort and for combatting social influence.<br /> <br /> Heroic mortals have access to three additional resources: Endurance, Focus, and Passion. A mortal\u2019s Endurance pool equals the sum of her Physical Attributes, her Focus pool is equal to the sum of her Mental Attributes, and her Passion pool is equal to the sum of her Social Attributes. They can also learn Feats, which allow them to spend their resources to enhance their dice rolls and perform extraordinary actions. Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is a Feat, available to mortals, as are various forms of thaumaturgy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Exalted have access to two additional resources: Essence and the Anima Banner. An Exalt\u2019s Essence pool depends upon what type of Exalt she is; A Solar\u2019s Essence pool is equal to her Essence score x10. Essence can be spent in place of Endurance, Focus, or Passion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An Exalt\u2019s Anima Banner is both a visual display and a source of power. The Anima Banner has five levels of activity, beginning with simply displaying her Caste Mark and culminating in a beacon of light visible for miles and a display characteristic of her nature. Initially invisible, an Exalt can choose to flare her Anima Banner to the next level once per round. Each round of combat, an Exalt recovers a number of motes of Essence equal to the level of her Anima Banner.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An Exalt can also learn Charms, which allow the Exalt to achieve supernatural levels of results with her actions. Most Charms cost some amount of Essence in order to activate. Charms can also cost levels from the Exalt\u2019s Anima Banner, though she cannot spend levels of her Anima Banner during any round in which she flares her Anima Banner and vice versa. Some Charms don\u2019t require that the Exalt expend levels of Anima Banner, but do require that the Exalt\u2019s Anima Banner be at or above a particular level in order to function.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In order to keep dice pools under control, all characters, mortal and Exalt, have a limit to the number of dice they can add to any given roll through Feats and Charms. This limit is called the Exertion Limit and is a ten dice. Additional successes added to a roll count as two dice. The only exception to this limit are dice or successes declared as Effortless.</span></span><br /> <br /> Character Creation uses exponential costs for buying Abilities, Attributes, and so on, making it cheaper to specialize only to a limited degree rather than start with 5s in anything you intend to invest heavily in.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With all that in place, the primary advantage that young Exalts would have over mortals is endurance in a fight, not crushingly high numbers. That band of named and backstoried bounty hunters after the players can all have unique, mechanically-backed fighting styles while that group of soldiers over there can still be mechanically simple and easy to run as a battle group.<br /> <br /> Implementing this, of course, involves rewriting most of the Charms chapter and a good portion of the Traits chapter, which is a daunting prospect. I've done similar things before, but it takes a while. Is this idea something anyone would like to see? Any issues this would cause? Too much complexity in play for not enough gain? Anything I seem to be overlooking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T03:33:23-08:00","id":1436775,"title":"","content":"So you've taken the essence pool down to what a godblooded has in vanilla, but added three more pools to compensate. Might be a bit much to juggle.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could just slam the pools together for exalts? they do have charms to think about after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T08:29:13-08:00","id":1436810,"title":"","content":"It seems like it's going to be too mechanically complex for me to use.<br /> <br /> STing a game, I'm not going to be tracking three mote pools for my mortal NPCs plus Willpower.<br /> <br /> But it seems like an interesting hack for mortal PCs, there's a lot you can hang off that.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I went the other way. Rolled Willpower and Essence together to make a single stat - Power. Gods, Exalted, Mortals, whatever, just has one Power Pool to spend from. The Exalted have a bigger pool, so their advantage is (like with your proposal) endurance.<br /> <br /> You lose a lot of granularity my way, but it's easier for new players to learn and less book-keeping for an ST to run. YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T09:12:08-08:00","id":1436818,"title":"","content":"So, roughly speaking, everyone gets essence pools, charms, and excellencies, but mortal pools are smaller and their charms weaker than Dragonblooded tier? And Anima becomes a deliberate power-up rather than a consequence of power use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T09:35:21-08:00","id":1436823,"title":"","content":"It really feels like you're reinventing the wheel here. This seems like a lot of work that's retreading ground already covered, what's the benefit you see this bringing that giving certain mortals a small mote pool and some low-power charms / die-adders wouldn't provide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T12:24:13-08:00","id":1436860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1436818#post1436818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, roughly speaking, everyone gets essence pools, charms, and excellencies, but mortal pools are smaller and their charms weaker than Dragonblooded tier? And Anima becomes a deliberate power-up rather than a consequence of power use?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty good summary. I would characterize Feats as being the foundation of Charms for all Exalts, so everyone has the same baseline of competence in all areas and Charms can build off of them.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1436775#post1436775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you've taken the essence pool down to what a godblooded has in vanilla, but added three more pools to compensate. Might be a bit much to juggle.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could just slam the pools together for exalts? they do have charms to think about after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect that in combat, you'll only really be tracking expenditures from one pool primarily. While some Feats might be spending Focus to negate some penalties for wind or spending Passion to rally troops, the majority of swinging swords better, dodging blows faster, and enduring blows would come from Endurance. If they are extremely focused on social or mental tasks, they might just be incapable of enhancing any of their combat rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1436823#post1436823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really feels like you're reinventing the wheel here. This seems like a lot of work that's retreading ground already covered, what's the benefit you see this bringing that giving certain mortals a small mote pool and some low-power charms / die-adders wouldn't provide?</div> </div> </div> </div>Common competency across Exalt types, more support and more engaging play for mortal games, setting verisimilitude, a common resource for Storytellers to pull those &quot;low-power Charms&quot; from, and a place for &quot;How is this magical?&quot; effects to go.<br /> <br /> One of the idea fragments that went into this idea was that concept floated during Ex3's development that mortals practicing particular Martial Arts styles would have access to Merits that would allow them to fight differently than each other in mechanically supported ways. This was dropped because it just doesn't work well when the only resources that a mortal has to spend in a fight are Initiative and Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T05:53:01-08:00","id":1436979,"title":"","content":"It feels to me like your arguement is with the setting rather than the rules? You're proposing one where the Exalted start out parallel to, maybe slight better than, &quot;interesting&quot; mortals, and then grow from there. That's very much not how Creation is presented. At the moment of Exaltation, you instantly become head, shoulders, and half a torso above your mortal former peers.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say it's a bad or uninteresting idea. But in that context, I feel like you could just build interesting mortals as Essence 1 Solars or Lunars, with more modest stats, no &quot;signature&quot; stuff (anima/shapechanging/etc), and reduced mote pools, and call it a day? The E1 range of Charms are generally supposed to be the &quot;pulp&quot; power level, though in 3e maybe you'd want to go through and explicitly tag Charms with &quot;Mortal-OK&quot; just to be sure.<br /> <br /> Not coincidentally this is kinda-sorta what 2e did with Half-Castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T06:25:35-08:00","id":1436986,"title":"","content":"Isn't the general consensus that what 2e did with half castes was a terrible idea though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T06:33:05-08:00","id":1436988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1436986#post1436986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the general consensus that what 2e did with half castes was a terrible idea though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not least of which was using a real world slur as a name. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T09:26:16-08:00","id":1437001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1436986#post1436986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the general consensus that what 2e did with half castes was a terrible idea though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lioness rightfully points out that the name itself is insensitive and problematic. It's something I myself tend to forget (the original slur isn't part of my dialect and Exalted was the first place I saw it), but given this reminder I'm going to endeavor to say &quot;Celestial-blooded&quot; instead.<br /> <br /> As for the system/setting problems associated with the concept itself... yes, there was a lot to not like, but I wouldn't say all of that is relevant here. <br /> <br /> On the fluff side, I'm not talking about literal Celestial-blooded, but rather about cribbing some low-level mechanics from the Exalted splats to represent a middle tier of &quot;advanced mortals&quot;. Like the renowned mortal doctor whose mundane skill is <i>mechanically </i>Ailment-Rectifying Method, or the famous mortal sea-captain who &quot;knows&quot; Salty Dog Method. Not because they're Solars but because they're the archetypical experts the Solar's powers reference. Master Horseman's Tehchnique's starts with the line &quot;The Exalt has the talent of a veteran equestrian&quot;; the idea here is just to borrow the mechanics to represent an <i>actual veteran equestrian</i>.<br /> <br /> On the mechanics side... yeah, there's work to applying this idea. I'd start with a blanket statement like &quot;Essence 1 only, increase Ability mins by +2, no excellencies&quot; and then see what problems remain. Like, even the lowest-level Solar Occult Charms are probably too supernatural for a mortal, for example. This type of blanket ruling is what made the Celestial-blooded so problematic, because the Celestial Charm sets weren't balanced with this kind of idea in mind back then either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T10:22:38-08:00","id":1437007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437001#post1437001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the fluff side, I'm not talking about literal Celestial-blooded, but rather about cribbing some low-level mechanics from the Exalted splats to represent a middle tier of &quot;advanced mortals&quot;. Like the renowned mortal doctor whose mundane skill is <i>mechanically </i>Ailment-Rectifying Method, or the famous mortal sea-captain who &quot;knows&quot; Salty Dog Method. Not because they're Solars but because they're the archetypical experts the Solar's powers reference. Master Horseman's Tehchnique's starts with the line &quot;The Exalt has the talent of a veteran equestrian&quot;; the idea here is just to borrow the mechanics to represent an <i>actual veteran equestrian</i>.<br /> <br /> On the mechanics side... yeah, there's work to applying this idea. I'd start with a blanket statement like &quot;Essence 1 only, increase Ability mins by +2, no excellencies&quot; and then see what problems remain. Like, even the lowest-level Solar Occult Charms are probably too supernatural for a mortal, for example. This type of blanket ruling is what made the Celestial-blooded so problematic, because the Celestial Charm sets weren't balanced with this kind of idea in mind back then either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a good idea.<br /> <br /> On Solar Occcut: letting a mortal exorcist see dematrialized spirts sounds okay. Spirit-Manifesting Word might even be okay.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with mortals getting one &quot;charm&quot; (as something like a five dot merit, like Terrestrial Circle Sorcery), so long as Solars still get 15 Charms and Excellencies.<br /> <br /> Yes, your mortal sea-captain knows Salty Dog Method. My Solar has Excellent Sail, knows Salty Dog Method <i>and </i>14 other Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T11:20:05-08:00","id":1437011,"title":"","content":"OK, so, I'm confused. This is supposed to be about improving mortal opposition/antagonists, aka NPCs, right?<br /> <br /> Because these rules feel like they're meant for giving mortal PCs more widgets.<br /> <br /> While we have zero guidance on taking the concept further, mortal NPCs can have Merits that grant them similar-to-but-worse effects as low level Charms. The Bride of Ahlat QC stats let them perform a pre-battle ritual, spend a WP, and get double 9s for three rolls or as a BG get Might 1 for the whole fight.<br /> <br /> It doesn't feel like we need the interesting but intense system of the OP for NPCs (though that looks interesting for expanding heroic mortal play), but rather something more like Storypath's NPC building rules where there's a more standardized set of traits you can layer on top of the base QC stats to specialize them a bit from the core templates.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T12:21:39-08:00","id":1437025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1436979#post1436979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels to me like your arguement is with the setting rather than the rules? You're proposing one where the Exalted start out parallel to, maybe slight better than, &quot;interesting&quot; mortals, and then grow from there. That's very much not how Creation is presented. At the moment of Exaltation, you instantly become head, shoulders, and half a torso above your mortal former peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still proposing that the Exalted tower over mortals in terms of accomplishment. The path that young Exalts take to that accomplishment, however, requires them to overcome opposition from mortals, not just ignore mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437001#post1437001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the mechanics side... yeah, there's work to applying this idea. I'd start with a blanket statement like &quot;Essence 1 only, increase Ability mins by +2, no excellencies&quot; and then see what problems remain. Like, even the lowest-level Solar Occult Charms are probably too supernatural for a mortal, for example. This type of blanket ruling is what made the Celestial-blooded so problematic, because the Celestial Charm sets weren't balanced with this kind of idea in mind back then either.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437007#post1437007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a problem with mortals getting one &quot;charm&quot; (as something like a five dot merit, like Terrestrial Circle Sorcery), so long as Solars still get 15 Charms and Excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think you've both missed the point here. Have you read through a couple pages of &quot;My Problem With Chargen&quot;? It's quite the multi-faceted discussion, but one of the points is that 90% of printed antagonists are unable to challenge most characters, partially because it is so easy to obtain resting defense values beyond what most printed antagonists can muster, which is a problem partly due to how costs are structured at character creation and partly because antagonists can't boost their own numbers, and a second point is that non-Exalted humans are bland - no matter how interesting their backstories are, they all are similar bags of numbers with no tricks. I agree with those two points and so &quot;no excellencies&quot; and &quot;only one Charm&quot; both defeat my attempts to address those points.<br /> <br /> In addition, you both acknowledge that &quot;Essence 1 Charms&quot; still aren't always something that should be within the grasp of mortals. You need to pick and choose, which means you essentially are creating a set of things that highly skilled mortals can accomplish versus a set of things that are outright magical. You are starting to walk the path that leads to something like my proposal, you just haven't taken all the steps yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T14:04:38-08:00","id":1437041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437025#post1437025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you've both missed the point here. Have you read through a couple pages of &quot;My Problem With Chargen&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... yes?<br /> <br /> My suggestion was you fix the challenge issue by not letting PCs max out seven different abilities at character creation and instead take one, or at most two, stats at 5 that represent the thing central to the character's concept.<br /> <br /> Then mortals could still challenge you by playing their strengths against your weaknesses.<br /> <br /> A Dawn can still cut down an elite soldier, but they can't also out-seduce a champion manipulator, and outhink a great philosopher -- at least not without blowing a bunch of motes on using their super-powers.<br /> <br /> A Twilight might reasonably struggle against an elite soldier.<br /> <br /> An elite soldier shouldn't, really, really shouldn't, be able to challenge a Dawn in single combat. Exaltation, to me, is a qualitative thing. The Exalted are meant to be more powerful than mortals. That's the point of Exaltation. Starting Exalts should blow mortals away <i>in their area of focus</i>.<br /> <br /> The Overseer can beat Mr. Glass to pulp. Mr. Glass doesn't need +10 dice in combat. Mr. Glass needs The Overseer to not be Intelligence 5 Wits 5 Integrity 5 in addition to being unbreakable with clairvoyance and super strength.<br /> <br /> And giving an NPC a cool widget (like the Bride of Ahlat's double-9s or a single Solar Charm) plays into that. The general principle of Solar Charms representing excellence and outstanding mortals having a mechanical widget to represent that is appealling to me. (The general principle of tagging charms Mortal-OK probably needs a bit of work.)<br /> <br /> As I said in my first reply, your system seems cool -- it looks like a great tool for Mortal PCs. But it's a lot of bookkeeping for NPCs: I'm not tracking <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Endurance, Focus, Passion</span></span>, Willpower, Initiative, and Health levels for every NPC in a scene, with Anima and Essence on top for Exalts. I'd love to see it, it sounds like a cool system. But, like, I don't even track a Blood Ape's mote pool. I'm not going to track a Mercenary Leader's Endurance, Focus, and Passsion.<br /> <br /> I like your idea of Feats -- that excites me, and I think Essence 1 Solar Charms could be a good base for that. I like the idea of anima as a generator. I like your exhertion cap.<br /> <br /> I'm neutral on your idea of exponential costs as a fix to character creation -- I don't think it <i>won't</i> work, I just don't think it's neccessary and it seems overly punitive for folks who want to play a high-powered &quot;And I'll Form the Head&quot; style game. (Who, perhaps ironically, would be those with the most to gain from hyping up mortals with a psuedo-Excellency.)<br /> <br /> I really don't think the solution to &quot;the numbers are too big&quot; is to say &quot;well make the other numbers bigger&quot;. Your numbers provide a lot more granularity, but in play... how is it different from just adding a static +10 dice to mortal statlines? I'm not convinced that's a solution. But it is a really neat idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-26-2021, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T16:46:45-08:00","id":1437057,"title":"","content":"The quick and dirty boost I'd consider for More Better Mortals is giving them 3 boosted rolls per scene, where the boost is (+Attribute) dice, in one set Attribute.<br /> <br /> It's barely more paperwork than willpower, but will make them competitive with Exalts just long enough to not be completely worthless.<br /> It wouldn't make them actually rival Exalts, but should at least give low-essence players a moment to go &quot;Oh he's pretty good&quot;, which is all I'd want it for.<br /> <br /> Occasionally I'd give 'em one charm to make things interesting or an artifact with 1-2 Evocations that can be used once.<br /> If I want more than that, I'm not talking about a Mortal anymore. If I specifically want a Mortal that can rival Exalts, that is a plot all of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T15:53:20-08:00","id":1437157,"title":"","content":"\u201cThoughts about improving the quality of mortal opposition\u201d<br /> <br /> *rewrites the whole freaking book*<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t remember what the real expression for this is so I\u2019m going to call it \u201cShooting a can with a nuke.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T19:17:52-08:00","id":1437184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437041#post1437041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think the solution to &quot;the numbers are too big&quot; is to say &quot;well make the other numbers bigger&quot;. Your numbers provide a lot more granularity, but in play... how is it different from just adding a static +10 dice to mortal statlines? I'm not convinced that's a solution. But it is a really neat idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping an Excellency-like effect available isn't the main point - I'm thinking more about feats for bypassing a portion of armor by shooting through an eyeslit, rolling to your feet when knocked down, and so on - but the way that the game's math works is that if you can't get within 5 dice of what you are fighting you are going to collapse hard once you have it's attention. That means putting 5/5/1 plus half-sized excellency within the reach of a master swordsman.<br /> <br /> Once the swordsman tires out three rounds later after putting his all out in trying to match the Dawn's skill, he can fold like a house of cards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437157#post1437157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThoughts about improving the quality of mortal opposition\u201d<br /> <br /> *rewrites the whole freaking book*<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t remember what the real expression for this is so I\u2019m going to call it \u201cShooting a can with a nuke.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at my signature. I'm the guy who rewrote the ghost rules twice because I didn't like how they were treated in 2e. Overkill is a normal reaction for me.<br /> <br /> Besides, if I was rewriting the whole book, I'd be making more changes than that, like tossing Appearance and changing the difficulties the system expects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T15:07:30-08:00","id":1437288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437025#post1437025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you've both missed the point here. Have you read through a couple pages of &quot;My Problem With Chargen&quot;? It's quite the multi-faceted discussion, but one of the points is that 90% of printed antagonists are unable to challenge most characters, partially because it is so easy to obtain resting defense values beyond what most printed antagonists can muster, which is a problem partly due to how costs are structured at character creation and partly because antagonists can't boost their own numbers, and a second point is that non-Exalted humans are bland - no matter how interesting their backstories are, they all are similar bags of numbers with no tricks. I agree with those two points and so &quot;no excellencies&quot; and &quot;only one Charm&quot; both defeat my attempts to address those points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm only pointing out that, to my mind, three editions of setting material says these &quot;antagonists&quot; <i>shouldn't</i> be a challenge for characters, so &quot;don't pretend mortals belong in the antagonists chapter&quot; would be a more internally consistent solution than &quot;buff mortals until they can provide meaningful opposition&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, I understand your perspective, and I see the appeal of young Exalts starting significantly, but not overwhelmingly, stronger than mortal opposition. The setting also insists that the beings who make <i>good</i> antagonists for young Exalts are relatively rare too, so it feels contrived that the bandit leader always just so happens to be an Outcaste DB, or that the giant squirrels giving your crafter friend trouble are really forest spirits, or whatever.<br /> <br /> But, like... the Dragon-blooded book shows us a young, maybe not chargen, Solar making a credible (if unsuccessful) assassination attempt on *Em-Effing Mnemon*, and another handily defeating a veteran Realm magistrate? So I think a world where mortals even show up in that conversation looks way different from Creation. Maybe for the better! Depends on the game you want to play. I think there is room for a more JRPG-ish game on the Exalted engine, where the starting protagonists are more defined by their potential than by their sudden overwhelming power. Something where you start out defeating guards and giant rats, and the final boss looks more like a 3rd Circle demon, a primordial, a Deathlord, or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437025#post1437025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, you both acknowledge that &quot;Essence 1 Charms&quot; still aren't always something that should be within the grasp of mortals. You need to pick and choose, which means you essentially are creating a set of things that highly skilled mortals can accomplish versus a set of things that are outright magical. You are starting to walk the path that leads to something like my proposal, you just haven't taken all the steps yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't expect I would take the remainder, because of the additional complexity. Since we're talking about NPCs you don't <i>really</i> have to tag everything &quot;Mortal-OK&quot;, you just print a general guideline that says &quot;E1 Charms are a good place to mine mechanics when you want your most impressive mortals to have something a little special&quot;. and give some examples, like the Brides.<br /> <br /> I think I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> that making mortal numbers bigger doesn't seem like the best solution to Exalt numbers being too big. if you want starting Exalts to be more like mortals, it makes more sense (to me) to bring <i>down</i> starting Exalts than to bring <i>up</i> the mortals. If you bring up mortals, you've bought yourself what, a bit more antagonist variety until Essence 2, when the Exalts run away with it again? Whereas if you tamp down the Exalts, you make the whole ramp a bit shallower.<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;heroic mortal&quot; chargen plus: 1-2 &quot;free&quot; starting Charms; nerf excellencies, supernal, mote pools, and mote regen; etc. This approaches your mortal problem from the other direction; mortals don't need all sorts of extra complexity to be meaningful opposition, because having good stats is enough for a while. And you'll have some time where &quot;mortals + E1 Charm-Merits&quot; is good enough after that.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that veered back into &quot;problems with chargen&quot; territory. I think at the end of the day what I'm trying to get across is, it seems like in your heroic mortal rules, you're effectively designing a new type of NPC-only &quot;Lesser Exalt&quot; to fill a very real opposition-for-young-Exalts niche that's not currently well served. I see echoes of Fair Folk (especially Commoners), with their Assumptions, Graces, and Gossamer. Which could absolutely be a cool set of rules! But in Creation-as-it-stands, I'm not in love with the idea that these rules are for experienced-but-not-&quot;special&quot; mortals, I would be more likely to use them to describe some new class of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-27-2021, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T18:36:32-08:00","id":1437308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437288#post1437288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, like... the Dragon-blooded book shows us a young, maybe not chargen, Solar making a credible (if unsuccessful) assassination attempt on *Em-Effing Mnemon*, and another handily defeating a veteran Realm magistrate?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with that is that Nova is a Solar assassin. Not a Solar who's attempting to assassinate somebody, she's a Solar who's specialized in assassinations. Same with that magistrate, the Solar she's fighting is a Dawn, he's definitely a fighter. What if Novia were to try and match the socialize ability of an epic mortal socialite, or if that Dawn were to try and bargain against a legendary guild prince?<br /> <br /> Should they just bowl over them because they're Solars and Solars beat mortals?<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't have to be like DnD, where a super legendary bard with +15 performance must also level 20 with level 9 spells and 150hp and a +8 attack bonus at least. Which works okay for DnD anyway because DnD's social system is <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uefCtOuhjKYxHYyAUzCE_63BmG_AMgvhh_DWYVy59Hg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T00:12:58-08:00","id":1437328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437288#post1437288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm only pointing out that, to my mind, three editions of setting material says these &quot;antagonists&quot; <i>shouldn't</i> be a challenge for characters, so &quot;don't pretend mortals belong in the antagonists chapter&quot; would be a more internally consistent solution than &quot;buff mortals until they can provide meaningful opposition&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. 1E explicitly says that a mob of mortals is dangerous to Solars. So, whilst I don't think one Elite Soldier should be given +5 dice to keep up with a Dawn, I do think that a lynch mob should be a threat to the Twilight when they shout &quot;BURN THE WITCH!&quot;<br /> <br /> The 3E corebook even states &quot;Even a lowly mortal hero armed with a knife may strike down one of the Solar Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Only, if you build 551+medium weapon+Stunt for resting Parry 8, Full Excellency+Willpower Parry 14... no they can't.<br /> <br /> In the Solar's area of focus, they should breeze over the greatest mortal hero. But printing four pages of mortal antagonists isn't a mistake that 3E made. An army of battleready soldiers should be a threat to any character who isn't combat focused. That Resolve 4 monk should be basically unshakable for any character that doesn't have Presence Charms.<br /> <br /> The books tell us mortals should matter. (Except 2E. 2E absolutely presented mortals as batteries.)<br /> <br /> But the whole point of Exaltation is giving mortals the powers of the gods to let them realise miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-28-2021, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T03:39:48-08:00","id":1437336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437328#post1437328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 3E corebook even states &quot;Even a lowly mortal hero armed with a knife may strike down one of the Solar Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Only, if you build 551+medium weapon+Stunt for resting Parry 8, Full Excellency+Willpower Parry 14... no they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the intent of what you quoted. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 Core page 190</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because decisive attacks are the result of seizing the Initiative provided by withering attacks, the quality of the combatants\u2019 arms has only a limited effect on their outcome. Even a lowly mortal hero armed with a knife may strike down one of the Solar Exalted, should the battle have brought him to the right moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T07:19:40-08:00","id":1437347,"title":"","content":"Also, it doesn't matter how high the Solar can raise his Parry normally, if he's asleep when the &quot;lowly mortal&quot; with a knife sneaks into his tent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T08:01:13-08:00","id":1437354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437336#post1437336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=Helvetica]<br /> <br /> That's not the intent of what you quoted. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If your lowly mortal has 400 initiative, they can't strike down a Solar with 14 Parry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T09:49:39-08:00","id":1437359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437308#post1437308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with that is that Nova is a Solar assassin. Not a Solar who's attempting to assassinate somebody, she's a Solar who's specialized in assassinations. Same with that magistrate, the Solar she's fighting is a Dawn, he's definitely a fighter.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agreed, same page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437308#post1437308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Novia were to try and match the socialize ability of an epic mortal socialite, or if that Dawn were to try and bargain against a legendary guild prince?<br /> <br /> Should they just bowl over them because they're Solars and Solars beat mortals?<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't have to be like DnD, where a super legendary bard with +15 performance must also level 20 with level 9 spells and 150hp and a +8 attack bonus at least. Which works okay for DnD anyway because DnD's social system is <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uefCtOuhjKYxHYyAUzCE_63BmG_AMgvhh_DWYVy59Hg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is it exactly!!!<br /> <br /> In D&amp;D, the class progression table says that your level 20 bard <i>must</i> have 150hp and +8 base attack bonus, even if he spent all 20 of those levels doing nothing but playing magic songs on his lute. It also says he <i>can't </i>have a base attack <i>higher </i>than +8, even if he spent those 20 levels stabbing people with a knife. He can't cast Meteor Storm, or have an animal companion.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't create <i>exclusive </i>character types. The &quot;wizard&quot; can choose to be good in combat as well. The option is there to be no better than a mortal in a fight, but it's not exactly weird to me that I've never seen anyone choose it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-28-2021, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T10:40:56-08:00","id":1437367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437328#post1437328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. 1E explicitly says that a mob of mortals is dangerous to Solars. So, whilst I don't think one Elite Soldier should be given +5 dice to keep up with a Dawn, I do think that a lynch mob should be a threat to the Twilight when they shout &quot;BURN THE WITCH!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the mob, and the Twilight. Which is kind of the whole point.<br /> <br /> 2e's Scroll of Heroes gave us Jasara, a Twilight with 2/3/2 physical and exactly 0 combat Ability dots. An average mortal soldier would be more than her match, and she should be pretty nervous about that mob! Good thing she knows DoOB and Flight of Separation.<br /> <br /> But is it really a surprise that such a character is atypical? This is a kung-fu game and you die if your kung-fu is weak. Jasara <i>could</i> go the rest of her life without learning to fight, putting all of her XP into Lore , Occult, Craft, and spells. But said life is probably going to be short, if a below-average mugger could off her for walking down the wrong street? It would take a pretty special story to make such a character viable, so for my part I'm glad that a Solar has to actually <i>choose</i> for ordinary mortals to be a threat.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Kind of reminds me of the 1e Sidereals book's Background section, which prompted you to explain <i>lack</i> of Backgrounds, not just the ones you took dots in.<br /> <br /> Salary 0: &quot;No salary. Did you piss someone off or are they impounding it to pay some heinous court fee? You live in someone's back room, or in your office. You have to beg or crash a feast to eat&quot;<br /> <br /> Sifu 0: &quot;Your Sifu knows only a single supernatural martial-arts form and probably has only partial mastery of that. What did you do to get such a teacher?&quot;<br /> <br /> Creation is a dangerous place, and an Exalt who can't defend herself is like a Sidereal with no Salary; totally possible, but noteworthy enough to make you ask questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437328#post1437328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 3E corebook even states &quot;Even a lowly mortal hero armed with a knife may strike down one of the Solar Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Only, if you build 551+medium weapon+Stunt for resting Parry 8, Full Excellency+Willpower Parry 14... no they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> pointed out, the context of the quote is explaining that Decisive attacks are about <i>circumstance, </i>not power or weapons. And with 400 (or even a much more reasonable) initiative that mortal <i>can </i>absolutely be a threat in the right circumstance, but that's <i>not</i> &quot;the master Solar swordsman is standing there unencumbered with his sword pointed at your face,&quot; regardless of initiative. Disarm and Ambush come to mind as ways to bypass Parry and/or Dodge completely. Spending that initiative to start a grapple, then immediately aborting to a Decisive Slam. Teamwork to stack penalties so that you're not facing a full 14 PDV (Grapple, Prone, Clash, Onslaught...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-28-2021, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T11:00:50-08:00","id":1437368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437367#post1437367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the mob, and the Twilight. Which is kind of the whole point.<br /> <br /> 2e's Scroll of Heroes gave us Jasara, a Twilight with 2/3/2 physical and exactly 0 combat Ability dots. An average mortal soldier would be more than her match, and she should be pretty nervous about that mob! Good thing she knows DoOB and Flight of Separation.<br /> <br /> But is it really a surprise that such a character is atypical? This is a kung-fu game and you die if your kung-fu is weak. Jasara <i>could</i> go the rest of her life without learning to fight, putting all of her XP into Lore , Occult, Craft, and spells. But said life is probably going to be short, if a below-average mugger could off her for walking down the wrong street? It would take a pretty special story to make such a character viable, so for my part I'm glad that a Solar has to actually <i>choose</i> for ordinary mortals to be a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except in 3E, a Dex 1 Ability 0 character can take out a dozen armed men (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1423701#post1423701\">no, really</a>).<br /> <br /> Such a character as Jasara <i>shouldn't be </i>atypical in 3E. Of the six sample characters the game gives us, two of them have their main combat ability at 2 dots.<br /> <br /> It's not just the mortal antagonists: a combat focused Blood Ape only has as 11 dice attack. An Essence 5, artifact wielding nephrack, only has 13 dice. The difficulty dice chart is 1-5. The QC dicepools out-and-out says that more than 10 dice is supposed to be &quot;likely to defeat even specialized player characters if they're not equally optimized&quot; because 3 dots is called out as being the level of an expert professional or immediately noteworthy individual. Strength 3 makes you immediately noticably strong. Melee 3 makes you an expert swordsman above the level of a trained professional.<br /> <br /> The game tells you that an Exalt should be at 3-6 dice for &quot;moderate to significant investment&quot; (remarkable base prowess (attribute 3) and trained professional level (ability 2) falls nicely here) and that &quot;even Exalts will rarely have [7-10 dice] in more than a few areas&quot;.<br /> <br /> The whole Withering/Decisive split (and Crippling Injuries and the difficulty scale of the antagonists) really does mean that you don't die if your kung-fu is weak. Dipping Swallow Defence, a single Ox-Body, and Melee 1 as a favored Ability will see your character through nicely on Dex 3 (Parry 4 with a medium weapon and a stunt, boostable to 9 ignoring all penalities, or up to Parry 12 with mounted and Full Defence) -- unless you're fighting five Octavians every session. Heck, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1372266#post1372266\">this is what Martial Arts 3 Dex 3 (and two Charms) looks like</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> pointed out, the context of the quote is explaining that Decisive attacks are about <i>circumstance, </i>not power or weapons. And with 400 (or even a much more reasonable) initiative that mortal <i>can </i>absolutely be a threat in the right circumstance, but that's <i>not</i> &quot;the master Solar swordsman is standing there unencumbered with his sword pointed at your face,&quot; regardless of initiative. Disarm and Ambush come to mind as ways to bypass Parry and/or Dodge completely. Spending that initiative to start a grapple, then immediately aborting to a Decisive Slam. Teamwork to stack penalties so that you're not facing a full 14 PDV (Grapple, Prone, Clash, Onslaught...) </div> </div> </div>Dipping Swallow Defence is an entry charm for Solar Melee. Disarm, grapple, smashing all needs you to hit that Parry 14 first.<br /> <br /> Ambush, ambush, I'm with you on. Your Melee 5 Solar Swordfighter <i>shouldn't</i> also take Wits 5 Awareness 5 so they can still be ambushed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-28-2021, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T11:38:01-08:00","id":1437371,"title":"","content":"I was going to reply but JohnDoe said everything I was going to but better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437368#post1437368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ambush, ambush, I'm with you on. Your Melee 5 Solar Swordfighter <i>shouldn't</i> also take Wits 5 Awareness 5 so they can still be ambushed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even this I find as rare. Maybe not Wits 5, I tend to see some Wits 3 going around sometimes, but Awareness 5 is a staple of standard chargen in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T12:58:09-08:00","id":1437381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437354#post1437354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If your lowly mortal has 400 initiative, they can't strike down a Solar with 14 Parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>14 Parry would be a pretty solid deterrent to another Solar, I don't worry about it because 10m 1wp is pretty unsustainable.<br /> <br /> The thing I see marginalise mortal opponents at my table is that my PCs tend to depend on their stunted defence and charms which they can activate after the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T14:43:19-08:00","id":1437391,"title":"","content":"copy-pasted from my Discord.<br /> <br /> So, I've been thinking;<br /> <br /> Originally when EX3 was pitched, the devs were wanting to include a robust 'technique' system for MA styles that were accessible for everyone and the exalted could expand upon with their charms. Ultimately, this design was scrapped because the people involved couldn't find a way to justify sets of effects accessible to the exalted that didn't just eat into their charm space (a least that's what I read when it was discussed).<br /> With the introduction of Lunars to the game's world and mechanics, perhaps this concern was less worrisome than it first appeared. Because we have a set of 'techniques' Exalted have access to (Lunars anyway) that are limited in their use so as to not overtake charm space. And those are Animal traits.<br /> <br /> Now, verisimilitude question- why do animals have access to charm-lite effects but Humans for some reason do not? They are both natural creatures that need to occupy the same world, but Animals for some reason have access to 'I can't believe it's not magic' (as defined by low essence charms) where Humans are left in the lurch. I don't know if I personally have the wherewithal to actually plot this out as a whole system- but the thought is in my head and I wanted to run it by people none the less.<br /> <br /> Open up Animal traits to be just 'traits' that any character can purchase. Leave them restricted in their use, so certain traits are only accessible in certain situations (like attacking from stealth) or with certain features (like wings). let these traits cost like... the same as charms. why not? 10exp. (kinda just cribbing lunars here) Let MA styles bundle together a set of traits themed to their style that people can access at a reduced cost, or with some other catch that makes them more easily accessible.<br /> <br /> Now, the big question- Do these traits now take over small details like dice adders and dice tricks to free up charm space to concentrate on actual power effects and abilities? Or do Exalted retain their dice trick charms so they have more universal access to those tricks without having to jump through the same hoops as mortals but at the cost of a few motes? Does this dilute Lunar's nieche too much? (I don't think so, but its a potential concern)<br /> <br /> The latter requires less re-writing but retains some of the charm bloat or hurdle charm issues some people have with the system the way it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T15:52:20-08:00","id":1437399,"title":"","content":"Iirc that was an early draft of their intentions for MAs: Essenceless techniques separate from charms.<br /> <br /> I don't think it hurts Lunars much, and it has the benefit of opening up heartsblood-tutoring that isn't eye-wateringly expensive due to being mostly charm focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T23:24:01-08:00","id":1437431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437391#post1437391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">copy-pasted from my Discord.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it.<br /> <br /> I don't think it dilutes the Lunar niche.<br /> If we were to start with Martial Arts, we could crib out the lower level &quot;Latent&quot; Traits and bundle those, leaving the native Exalted charmless untouched.<br /> <br /> (Thematically, I think the reason animals get these abilities is that the game is tuned to human baseline and these are meant to be abilities humans don't have.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-01-2021, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T04:07:36-08:00","id":1437455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437391#post1437391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">copy-pasted from my Discord.<br /> <br /> So, I've been thinking;<br /> <br /> Originally when EX3 was pitched, the devs were wanting to include a robust 'technique' system for MA styles that were accessible for everyone and the exalted could expand upon with their charms. Ultimately, this design was scrapped because the people involved couldn't find a way to justify sets of effects accessible to the exalted that didn't just eat into their charm space (a least that's what I read when it was discussed).<br /> With the introduction of Lunars to the game's world and mechanics, perhaps this concern was less worrisome than it first appeared. Because we have a set of 'techniques' Exalted have access to (Lunars anyway) that are limited in their use so as to not overtake charm space. And those are Animal traits.<br /> <br /> Now, verisimilitude question- why do animals have access to charm-lite effects but Humans for some reason do not? They are both natural creatures that need to occupy the same world, but Animals for some reason have access to 'I can't believe it's not magic' (as defined by low essence charms) where Humans are left in the lurch. I don't know if I personally have the wherewithal to actually plot this out as a whole system- but the thought is in my head and I wanted to run it by people none the less.<br /> <br /> Open up Animal traits to be just 'traits' that any character can purchase. Leave them restricted in their use, so certain traits are only accessible in certain situations (like attacking from stealth) or with certain features (like wings). let these traits cost like... the same as charms. why not? 10exp. (kinda just cribbing lunars here) Let MA styles bundle together a set of traits themed to their style that people can access at a reduced cost, or with some other catch that makes them more easily accessible.<br /> <br /> Now, the big question- Do these traits now take over small details like dice adders and dice tricks to free up charm space to concentrate on actual power effects and abilities? Or do Exalted retain their dice trick charms so they have more universal access to those tricks without having to jump through the same hoops as mortals but at the cost of a few motes? Does this dilute Lunar's nieche too much? (I don't think so, but its a potential concern)<br /> <br /> The latter requires less re-writing but retains some of the charm bloat or hurdle charm issues some people have with the system the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's doable.<br /> <br /> The main criticism I had with Techniques during the playtest was that they were too structured. Snake and Tiger Style each had their own charm like abilities and the ones associated with Snake Style seemed much more useful if you were a mortal fighting against someone with access to dice adders. Also that 6 mortal level techniques before each style would increase the buy-in cost for people who wanted to roleplay being a great martial artist prior to Exaltation but subsequently never use them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T05:38:53-08:00","id":1437464,"title":"","content":"Maybe they could have just made the essence 1 charms be buyable by mortals and have a base effect that was free or cost WP and then a more powerful effect (or upgrade to the base version) that cost essence to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T19:03:56-08:00","id":1437565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437464#post1437464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they could have just made the essence 1 charms be buyable by mortals and have a base effect that was free or cost WP and then a more powerful effect (or upgrade to the base version) that cost essence to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem unreasonable, just a yet-lower-powered iteration of the Terrestrial Keyword would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T05:06:12-08:00","id":1437795,"title":"","content":"Would probably require re-working the styles a bit though. I tried to mortal-keyword the essence 1 snake style charms and it quickly became clear that there wasn't much space for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T05:25:45-08:00","id":1437798,"title":"","content":"<b>New Keywords</b><br /> <br /> Mortal-OK: Mortals may buy this Charm. They may spend Initiative instead of motes (on a one-to-one basis) to pay Charm costs. Some Mortal-OK charms list alternative costs that mortals may use to activate the Charm<br /> <br /> Enlightened: This Charm has additional effects when made by beings with an Essence pool.<br /> <br /> Serpentine Evasion<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Martial Arts 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Mastery, Uniform, Mortal-OK<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Ducking and weaving, the snake confounds predators\u2019 attempts at violence. Serpentine Evasion adds +1 to the martial artist\u2019s Evasion against a single attack.<br /> <br /> If the attack is made after the martial artist has already taken her turn that round, she may declare this Charm after the attack has already been rolled \u2014 enemies who cannot even keep pace with her in battle have no hope of striking her.<br /> <br /> Mastery: Successfully evading an attack after using this Charm cumulatively lowers the cost of subsequent activations of it by one mote until the martial artist\u2019s next turn.<br /> <br /> Striking Cobra Technique<br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual, Mastery, Enlightened, Mortal-OK<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The snake claims its victory not by striking hardest, but by striking first. Against an enemy with lower Initiative or who hasn\u2019t taken their turn yet this round, Striking Cobra Technique adds the martial artist\u2019s Dexterity to the raw damage of a withering attack, or one die to the raw damage of a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Enlightened: Against enemies in Initiative Crash, the withering damage boost is added after soak, while the decisive damage boost is converted to an automatic success.<br /> <br /> Mastery: Add the martial artist\u2019s (Essence + 2) to her Initiative when determining if she can use this Charm against an enemy.<br /> <br /> Snake Form<br /> Cost: 8m; Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Form, Enlightened, Mortal-OK<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Serpentine Evasion, Striking<br /> Cobra Technique<br /> <br /> The martial artist steps back into the posture of a wary snake\u2014head back, ready to attack or retreat. Her motions become sinuous and hypnotic, as mesmerizing as they are deadly. Enemies are entranced by this posture, taking a -1 penalty on attack rolls against her if their Initiative rating is lower than the martial artist\u2019s. In addition, this flexible pose makes it easier to roll with attacks and thus minimize their impact, adding the stylist\u2019s Dexterity rating to her soak.<br /> <br /> Enlightened: Instead all attackers take a -1 penalty, which increases to -3 if the attackers Initiative rating is lower than the martial artist\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Special activation rules: Whenever the martial artist makes a withering attack which lowers an enemy\u2019s current Initiative value from greater than her own to less than her own, she may reflexively activate Snake Form. Mortal users of Snake form only may assume Snake Form for only 1WP instead of 8i if using the Reflexive activation or activating the Form on their first action in a combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-03-2021, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T05:36:35-08:00","id":1437802,"title":"","content":"Striking Cobra Technique is hideously bad for mortals. The decisive version is obviously useless, netting you -2 damage on hit, but the withering version isn't much better off either - even in your best case scenario (you have 5 dex, you hit successfully, and you already have enough damage to punch through your opponent's soak) you can expect to gain 2.5i for a 3i investment. Ew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T05:48:26-08:00","id":1437804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1436756-thoughts-about-improving-the-quality-of-mortal-opposition?p=1437802#post1437802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Striking Cobra Technique is hideously bad for mortals. The decisive version is obviously useless, netting you -2 damage on hit, but the withering version isn't much better off either - even in your best case scenario (you have 5 dex, you hit successfully, and you already have enough damage to punch through your opponent's soak) you can expect to gain 2.5i for a 3i investment. Ew.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent would be to get a Withering damage boost a la chopping that might help you Crash an opponent. Remember, you might only be gaining 2.5i for your attack, but they're losing 2.5i (and these tricks aren't calibrated to the level of Solar Charms but to the dice tricks already available to mortals). Calibrate to taste.<br /> <br /> The decisive thing is just because I couldn't be bothered to copy-paste that section of charm out into the enlightened area. Too wordy for too little gain.<br /> <br /> And, of course, if you're using OPs idea for Endurance, Focus, and Passion you could pay with one of those instead of initiative. It's just meant to be illustrative.<br /> <br /> You could just let them have the Charm as printed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-03-2021, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}